  "limitations": [
    "Four measured samples per condition and workload are an engineering screen, not confidence intervals or p95 estimates. Every completed sample is retained; observed maxima are reported.",
    "Initial cache creation is retained separately and is not a cold-filesystem or cold-toolchain measurement. Full compilation plus tracing/hashing can cost more than the original builder.",
    "Implementation-only edit workloads preserve exported declarations. Changes to a core declaration dependency can require both packages to compile; no speed claim is made for that case.",
    "Background host load is recorded per sample. Earlier functional runs timed out during a much larger contention spike; those failures and the original-compiler attribution check are retained.",
    "TypeScript command-line execution is an internal export of the pinned 5.9.3 compiler. Changing that dependency requires these byte-comparison and functional gates.",
    "Receipts retain compiler-owned observations. A source edit after validation may allow the current build to finish; the next build rejects reuse against the changed input.",
    "Serialize builds within a checkout. Receipts are local, disposable build state under ignored workbench; they are not an authenticated remote cache.",
    "Full 203-command core verification was not rerun for this packaging-only change. Original emitted package bytes match; prior browser/Rust behavior evidence remains separate.",
    "No release, Chromium, Rust, E2E or native Linux performance claim. Native Linux remains unverified."
  ],
